comp('4.4.4','Hazardous materials awareness and response','Recognize and respond safely to hazardous materials in field operations',
 'Recognizes potential hazardous materials met in field work, protects self and others, and takes notification, isolation or containment actions within the limits of one training level and the organization emergency response plan. Span A + L1-L3; site remediation management is a separate competency. Qualification gate: HAZWOPER training at the level the position hazard assessment requires. v1 pairs emergency-response levels (Awareness/Operations/Technician) with site-worker course hours (24/40 h); IO judges this a content error for FC/CP to verify against 29 CFR 1910.120.')
ind('4.4.4','A','Identifies common field indicators of hazardous materials (containers, labels, placards, odors, stained soil, stressed vegetation) in a photo- or site-based exercise and states the required first action.','knowledge-test: recognition exercise','mode=unaided; use=select (minimum screen only)|develop; replaces v1 F K "Completes HAZWOPER Awareness training; recognizes common hazards" (B4 compound) and F I2; obs4=3')
ind('4.4.4','L1','Stops work, moves to a safe upwind and upslope distance, and notifies through the designated channel with location and observed indicators when a potential hazardous material is encountered.','simulation: drill observation scored against checklist','mode=unaided; use=select|develop; safety_or_legal_critical=true; replaces v1 F I4,I5; obs4=3')
ind('4.4.4','L1','Uses the safety data sheet or responder guidebook to determine protective actions for an identified substance before handling it.','work-product: practical test with reference materials','mode=assisted (reference tools); use=select; replaces v1 F I3 "Uses Safety Data Sheets (SDS) appropriately"; obs4=3')
ind('4.4.4','L2','Establishes an isolation zone and access control for a suspected release, using the responder guidebook, before any containment is attempted.','simulation: drill observation scored against checklist','mode=unaided; use=select; safety_or_legal_critical=true; replaces v1 I I4; obs4=3')
ind('4.4.4','L2','Contains a small identified release (e.g., fuel or oil) using the PPE and methods authorized for one training level, and documents the response.','simulation|record: drill observation; incident record','mode=unaided; use=select|develop; replaces v1 I I2 and A "Responds to hazmat incidents within training limits"; obs4=3')
ind('4.4.4','L3','Develops the hazardous-materials section of a field operations or site safety plan, specifying hazards, required training levels, PPE, notification chains and decontamination.','work-product: plan reviewed by safety officer','mode=assisted; use=promote; replaces v1 A I6; obs4=3')

