comp('5.2.1','Stakeholder identification and analysis','Identify and analyze affected parties for an environmental decision',
 'Identifies individuals, organizations, communities and governments affected by or able to affect an environmental decision, analyzes their interests, rights, relationships and influence, and uses the analysis to design differentiated engagement; it distinguishes sovereign governments, engaged through consultation, from stakeholders. Span L1-L4. The v1 database holds no indicators for this or any Domain 5 competency (parse defect); v1 source text lists Tribes as a stakeholder category, which TN should review.')
ind('5.2.1','L1','Compiles a party list for a project from designated sources (prior records, permit files, mailing lists, local directories), recording contact details, basis for inclusion and source for each entry.','work-product: list audit','mode=assisted; use=develop|select; replaces v1 source F "Creates stakeholder lists using obvious sources"; obs4=3')
ind('5.2.1','L2','Produces a stakeholder analysis for a defined project that records interests, concerns, relationships and influence for each party, including the methods used to reach groups absent from existing lists.','work-product: analysis scored with rubric','mode=assisted (AI search permitted; each party verified); use=select; replaces v1 source I indicators 1-4; obs4=3')
ind('5.2.1','L2','Distinguishes Tribal nations and other governments whose participation is by government-to-government consultation or legal right from stakeholders in the analysis, and routes them to the consultation process.','work-product|sjt: analysis review; scenario item','mode=assisted; use=select; jurisdiction_variable=true; new; TN to review wording; obs4=3')
ind('5.2.1','L3','Updates the stakeholder analysis as a contested decision evolves, documenting new parties, shifts in positions or coalitions, and resulting changes to the engagement plan.','work-product|interview: longitudinal case file; structured interview','mode=assisted; use=promote; attribute=complexity; replaces v1 source A "Anticipates coalition formation" (inferred) ; obs4=3')
ind('5.2.1','L3','Designs differentiated engagement strategies for parties with conflicting interests or unequal capacity to participate, stating how each identified participation barrier will be addressed.','work-product: strategy scored by SME panel','mode=assisted; use=promote; replaces v1 source I "Designs differentiated engagement strategies" (no standard) and A "Recognizes and addresses issues of representation and equity"; obs4=3')
ind('5.2.1','L4','Advises decision-makers on engagement strategy for a high-conflict decision in a written assessment that states the risks of each option to legitimacy, equity and decision durability.','work-product|interview: assessment memo (real or simulated case) plus interview','mode=assisted; use=promote (simulation allowed so the indicator is not opportunity-gated); replaces v1 source E "Advises on stakeholder strategies for major controversial projects" (O); obs4=3')

