ind('6.7.1','L2','Calculates cancer and non-cancer risk estimates for defined receptors and pathways using the agency accepted methods, documenting assumptions and inputs so that a reviewer can reproduce the result.','work-product: case dataset scored by re-performance','mode=assisted (calculation tools; verification required); use=select; replaces v1 I I2 "Uses risk assessment models (EPA IRIS, CalTOX, RAGS)" (T flag) and I3; obs4=3')
ind('6.7.1','L2','Identifies complete and incomplete exposure pathways for a site from a conceptual site model and data, justifying each determination.','work-product: case exercise','mode=assisted; use=select; replaces v1 F I4 "Assists with exposure pathway analysis" (B6) and I I4; obs4=3')
ind('6.7.1','L3','Characterizes uncertainty and variability in a risk estimate, identifying which inputs drive the result and how alternative defensible assumptions change it.','work-product|interview: sensitivity analysis plus structured interview','mode=assisted; use=promote; replaces v1 I I5 "Addresses uncertainty and variability" (B6); obs4=3')
ind('6.7.1','L3','Explains risk findings at an affected-community meeting in plain language, covering what is known, unknown and being done, and records questions that need follow-up.','simulation: role-play scored with BARS (community-member raters included)','mode=unaided; use=promote; v1 T3 tagged H/Hi/C; obs4=3')
ind('6.7.1','L4','Develops a site-specific or cumulative risk assessment approach where standard methods do not fit, documenting the departures and their scientific justification for peer review.','work-product: approach document plus peer-review record','mode=assisted; use=promote; replaces v1 A I3 and E "Shapes risk assessment science and policy" (B3); obs4=3')

comp('7.2.1','Validating AI outputs against ecological and regulatory ground truth','Validate AI-generated environmental work products',
 'Evaluates AI-generated analyses, classifications and documents against independent field, data and regulatory evidence before professional use, decides whether to accept, qualify or reject them, and documents the basis. Span A + L1-L4. Overlaps 7.2.3 at L3; CA to consider merging or sharpening the boundary.')
ind('7.2.1','L1','Applies the organization validation checklist to an AI-generated output (e.g., species list, habitat map, regulatory summary) and flags every item that fails or cannot be verified.','simulation|record: seeded-error exercise; checklist audit','mode=assisted; use=select|develop; replaces v1 F A "Performs structured checklist-based validation of AI outputs with guidance"; obs4=3')
ind('7.2.1','L2','Compares an AI-generated product against independent ground-truth or reference evidence and records an accept, qualify or reject decision with the evidence for each material element.','simulation: seeded-error work sample (score = detection rate and false-alarm rate)','mode=assisted; use=select; replaces v1 I A and I1,I4; obs4=3')
ind('7.2.1','L2','Checks every legal or regulatory citation in an AI-assisted analysis against the source text and corrects or removes any that are inaccurate or do not exist.','simulation: seeded fabricated and misquoted citations','mode=assisted; use=select; jurisdiction_variable=true; replaces v1 I I2; obs4=3')
ind('7.2.1','L3','Determines the conditions under which a specific AI tool outputs are reliable for an operational use by testing it across representative and edge cases, and documents the reliability envelope.','work-product|interview: validation study plus structured interview','mode=supervisory; use=promote; overlaps v1 7.2.3 I I1; obs4=3')
ind('7.2.1','L4','Sets validation acceptance criteria and sampling rates for AI-assisted workflows in a program, scaled to the consequence of error, and audits compliance with them.','work-product|record: criteria document; audit records','mode=supervisory; use=promote; replaces v1 A I1 and E "Shapes field-wide standards" (B3); obs4=3')

comp('7.1.3','Regulatory professional integrity','Maintain integrity of regulatory and scientific findings under institutional pressure',
 'Produces regulatory and scientific findings that accurately represent the evidence, including uncertainty and contrary evidence, discloses conflicts of interest, and uses documented channels when institutional pressure conflicts with professional obligations. Span A + L1-L4. Selection caution: assess only through work products and SJT items on procedures and obligations; never score integrity as a trait, and never ask about personal political views (see report.md section 2.4).')
ind('7.1.3','L1','Discloses actual or potential conflicts of interest in an assigned project through the organization disclosure procedure before work begins.','record|sjt: disclosure record; scenario items on the procedure','mode=unaided; use=develop|select (SJT only); replaces v1 F A "Identifies potential conflicts of interest… follows established disclosure procedures"; obs4=3')
ind('7.1.3','L2','Reports uncertainty, data limitations and evidence contrary to the preferred conclusion in a regulatory analysis, so that a reviewer can see what the evidence does not support.','work-product: review of the analysis against a seeded case','mode=assisted; use=select (work-sample form)|develop; replaces v1 I I3 "Communicates uncertainty and dissenting findings honestly" (trait-laden); obs4=3')
ind('7.1.3','L2','Records in the project file any direction received to change a technical finding or scope, with date, source, and the technical basis for any disagreement.','record: file audit; sjt','mode=unaided; use=develop; replaces v1 I I2; obs4=3')
ind('7.1.3','L3','Identifies which professional code provision and scientific-integrity policy applies to a contested situation and selects the escalation path the policy provides, in a case-based exercise.','sjt|interview: case analysis scored with BARS','mode=unaided; use=select|promote; replaces v1 I I1 and I4; note v1 cites "NEPA scientific integrity requirements", a reference IO judges should become jurisdiction-variable after 2025 NEPA changes (SC to confirm); obs4=3')
ind('7.1.3','L4','Designs review and documentation procedures for a program that make changes to technical findings traceable and reviewable, and tests them against past contested cases.','work-product|interview: procedure design plus test memo','mode=assisted; use=promote; replaces v1 A I1 and E "Recognized as a leading practitioner" (B3); obs4=3')

